Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WS-08: address review on 01d8023 and the #35 follow-up

- Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y and Ctrl+Shift+Z yield to text fields: a new
  Scope::OutsideText (canvas or a panel without a text field), so typing
  in F2 tag editing or the command field keeps the field's own undo.
- Smart duplicate: copied main contacts (a symbol switching two or more
  separate poles) make a new device even when the coil stays behind, so
  copying the main circuit gives -K2 poles instead of a second set on
  -K1. A lone auxiliary contact still stays with its device.
- Smart duplicate copies texts attached to copied symbols, junctions and
  wires (device tag and wire number labels) and attaches them to the
  copies; selected free texts are copied and moved by the offset.
- Copied devices are numbered in natural tag order (-K2 before -K10).
- Main circuit journey: one net fewer after the merge with #35, because
  the copied -X1:PE joins the original PE under the Join terminal rule.
- view.focus_mode is now view.focus; add view.pin_outline, matching the
  app shell and DESIGN.md.
- Cargo.lock: add novo-workflow after taking main's lock file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
